libglycin-gtk4: set a RUNPATH of $ORIGIN and the amber-gtk4 bundle

Upstream links libglycin-gtk4 with no RUNPATH. The Rust cdylib then resolves its NEEDED
libglycin-2.so.0 and libgtk-4.so.1 only through the loader's default search, which finds
neither the sibling library in /usr/lib/amber-glycin nor GTK 4.16 in /usr/lib/amber-gtk4:
it would load the distro's GTK 4.14, which lacks gdk_memory_texture_builder_*.

Measured: `readelf -d libglycin-gtk4-2.so.0 | grep -E 'RPATH|RUNPATH'` is empty before and
names both directories after.

--- a/libglycin/libglycin-gtk4/build.rs
+++ b/libglycin/libglycin-gtk4/build.rs
@@ -39,5 +39,9 @@
         _ => {}
     }
 
+    // Amber: RUNPATH, so the library finds libglycin-2 beside it and GTK in the
+    // amber-gtk4 bundle (as amber-vte does) rather than the distro's older one.
+    println!("cargo:rustc-cdylib-link-arg=-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN:/usr/lib/amber-gtk4");
+
     system_deps::Config::new().probe().unwrap();
 }
